IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-18.l4 -- ARTICLE 18 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT TO RESTRICTION OF PROCESSING (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 241-249 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 18 at 241-242 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN for the right and its four points, MAYBE `Duty outcome`
-- for the two duties, a DEONTIC for the regulative rule.
-- WHOSE.  Paragraph 1 is the data subject's CLAIM against the controller (correlative: the controller's duty to restrict).
-- Paragraph 2 binds the processing of restricted data (passive: no party is named, so a decision function only, fork F18-1).
-- Paragraph 3 names the controller and the act.  'Restriction of processing' is defined in Art 4(3) (the keel); this module
-- takes no input for it: the right is to "obtain restriction of processing" as Art 4(3) defines the act.
-- ARTICLE 11(2): see P2-art-15.l4.   THE POINTS follow the pattern of Art 6(1) in P1: each point answers JUST TRUE when it
-- holds and JUST FALSE when not, by inference from "where one of the following applies" (marginal reading (a)).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 18 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 18(1) restrict the processing of the personal data concerning the data subject`
    `Art 18(3) inform the data subject before the restriction of processing is lifted`

§ `Article 18(1): the four points`

-- src:244 | (a) the accuracy of the personal data is contested by the data subject, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy of the personal data;
@ref Art 18(1)(a) (src:244)
GIVEN `the accuracy of the personal data is contested by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is one enabling the controller to verify the accuracy of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1)(a) point (a) applies: the accuracy of the personal data is contested, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy` MEANS
    IF `the accuracy of the personal data is contested by the data subject` AND `the period is one enabling the controller to verify the accuracy of the personal data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "where one of the following applies: (a) the accuracy of the personal data is contested by the data subject, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy of the personal data"

-- src:245 | (b) the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes the erasure of the personal data and requests the restriction of their use instead;
@ref Art 18(1)(b) (src:245)
GIVEN `the processing is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject opposes the erasure of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject requests the restriction of their use instead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes erasure and requests restriction instead` MEANS
    IF `the processing is unlawful` AND `the data subject opposes the erasure of the personal data` AND `the data subject requests the restriction of their use instead`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(b) the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes the erasure of the personal data and requests the restriction of their use instead"

-- src:246 | (c) the controller no longer needs the personal data for the purposes of the processing, but they are required by the data subject for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims;
@ref Art 18(1)(c) (src:246)
GIVEN `the controller no longer needs the personal data for the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are required by the data subject for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1)(c) point (c) applies: the controller no longer needs the personal data but the data subject requires them for legal claims` MEANS
    IF `the controller no longer needs the personal data for the purposes of the processing` AND `the personal data are required by the data subject for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(c) the controller no longer needs the personal data for the purposes of the processing, but they are required by the data subject for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims"

-- src:247 | (d) the data subject has objected to processing pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the legitimate grounds of the controller override those of the data subject.
@ref Art 18(1)(d) (src:247)
GIVEN `the data subject has objected to processing pursuant to Article 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the verification whether the legitimate grounds of the controller override those of the data subject is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1)(d) point (d) applies: the data subject has objected pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the controller's grounds override` MEANS
    IF `the data subject has objected to processing pursuant to Article 21(1)` AND `the verification whether the legitimate grounds of the controller override those of the data subject is pending`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(d) the data subject has objected to processing pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the legitimate grounds of the controller override those of the data subject"

§ `Article 18(1): the right to restriction`

-- src:243 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing where one of the following applies:
@ref Art 18(1) chapeau (src:243)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 18(1)(a) point (a) applies: the accuracy of the personal data is contested, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 18(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes erasure and requests restriction instead` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 18(1)(c) point (c) applies: the controller no longer needs the personal data but the data subject requires them for legal claims` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 18(1)(d) point (d) applies: the data subject has objected pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the controller's grounds override` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF `Art 18(1)(a) point (a) applies: the accuracy of the personal data is contested, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 18(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes erasure and requests restriction instead` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 18(1)(c) point (c) applies: the controller no longer needs the personal data but the data subject requires them for legal claims` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 18(1)(d) point (d) applies: the data subject has objected pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the controller's grounds override` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 18(1)(a) point (a) applies: the accuracy of the personal data is contested, for a period enabling the controller to verify the accuracy` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 18(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is unlawful and the data subject opposes erasure and requests restriction instead` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 18(1)(c) point (c) applies: the controller no longer needs the personal data but the data subject requires them for legal claims` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 18(1)(d) point (d) applies: the data subject has objected pursuant to Article 21(1) pending the verification whether the controller's grounds override` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "where one of the following applies"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a point is not decided by the facts the caller gave, and none holds

-- src:243 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing where one of the following applies:
@ref Art 18(1): the controller's duty to restrict (src:243)
GIVEN `Art 18(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 18 action`
`Art 18(1) the controller must restrict the processing of the personal data` MEANS
    IF `Art 18(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 18(1) restrict the processing of the personal data concerning the data subject`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the text names the controller ("the right to obtain from the controller restriction of processing") and the act (restricting, as Art 4(3) defines it); no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path); the rule takes the answer of the right (R8)

§ `Article 18(2): the restricted data may be processed only as the paragraph allows`

-- src:248 | 2. Where processing has been restricted under paragraph 1, such personal data shall, with the exception of storage, only be processed with the data subject's consent or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims or for the protection of the rights of another natural or legal person or for reasons of important public interest of the Union or of a Member State.
@ref Art 18(2) (src:248)
GIVEN `the processing has been restricted under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is storage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject consents to the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is for the protection of the rights of another natural or legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is for reasons of important public interest of the Union or of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 18(2) the restricted personal data are processed, with the exception of storage, only with the data subject's consent or for one of the three purposes that paragraph 2 names` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processing has been restricted under paragraph 1`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where processing has been restricted under paragraph 1"
        IF `the processing is storage`
           OR `the data subject consents to the processing`
           OR `the processing is for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims`
           OR `the processing is for the protection of the rights of another natural or legal person`
           OR `the processing is for reasons of important public interest of the Union or of a Member State`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (a list closed with "only", the text says no in its own words): "such personal data shall, with the exception of storage, only be processed with the data subject's consent or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims or for the protection of the rights of another natural or legal person or for reasons of important public interest of the Union or of a Member State"

§ `Article 18(3): informing the data subject before the restriction is lifted`

-- src:249 | 3. A data subject who has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1 shall be informed by the controller before the restriction of processing is lifted.
@ref Art 18(3) (src:249)
GIVEN `the data subject has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller informed the data subject before the restriction of processing was lifted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 18(3) the controller informs the data subject who has obtained restriction of processing before the restriction is lifted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A data subject who has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1": a data subject without a restriction is outside the sentence, and it has no gate word (ruling (c))
        IF `the controller informed the data subject before the restriction of processing was lifted`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "shall be informed by the controller before the restriction of processing is lifted"

GIVEN `the data subject has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the restriction of processing is to be lifted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 18 action`
`Art 18(3) the controller must inform the data subject before the restriction of processing is lifted` MEANS
    IF `the data subject has obtained restriction of processing pursuant to paragraph 1`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 18(3) inform the data subject before the restriction of processing is lifted`
         WITHIN `the time at which the restriction of processing is to be lifted`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the data subject was not informed before the restriction of processing was lifted"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the clock counts from the moment the restriction is obtained; the limit is the instant at which the restriction is lifted ("before" is read as at or before that instant: marginal reading, fork F13-2)
